  "arrangement": "original, written for Stackapella on the harmony of the print's piano part (public domain, published with the song in 1924): the soprano sings the print's voice part a whole tone higher, with breaths written in for beginners; the alto, tenor and bass hum its chords",
  "recordings": "synthesized guides",
  "checked": null,
  "source": "Shorty George Blues, words by Geo. W. Thomas and Hociel Thomas, music by Geo. W. Thomas (Chicago: Geo. W. Thomas Music Co., copyright 1924 by Geo. W. Thomas), the copy stamped \"MAR 14 1924\", read from the scan at sheetmusicsinger.com: the voice part and the piano's chords, in F, written here a whole tone higher in G. The verses are the first chorus of stanza 1, both choruses of stanza 2 and both of stanza 3; the second chorus of stanza 1 and all of stanza 4 are left out, as are the piano introduction and the Dance Part"
